<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Evening Offices of the Church</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1760</span><span class="sg-chain-h">reprinted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">An Essay on the Church Plain Chant (Samuel Webbe)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1782</span><span class="sg-chain-h">reprinted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Additional Latin verses (Jean-François-Étienne Borderies)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">three new verses</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Herbei, o ihr Gläub'gen (Friedrich Heinrich Ranke)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1823</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (German)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">English translation (Frederick Oakeley)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1841</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation, later O Come, All Ye Faithful</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Come, All Ye Faithful (Murray's Hymnal)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1852</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation by Oakeley and William Thomas Brooke combined</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hither Ye Faithful, Haste with Songs of Triumph (Sacred Harp tradition)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1860</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same tune</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Parody of the chorus in Gargantua (François Rabelais)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1542</span><span class="sg-chain-h">evidence that the chorus was current before</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec"><h2>People, places and events</h2><div class="tih-tags"><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">John Francis Wade</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">John Reading</span><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-iv-of-portugal">John IV of Portugal</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonaventure">Bonaventure</a><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">François Rabelais</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Jean-François-Étienne Borderies</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Frederick Oakeley</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">William Thomas Brooke</span><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-edward-stuart">Charles Edward Stuart</a><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Bennett Zon</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">William H. Grattan Flood</span><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-frideric-handel">George Frideric Handel</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christoph-willibald-gluck">Christoph Willibald Gluck</a><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Marcos Portugal</span><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-arne">Thomas Arne</a><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Samuel Webbe</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Friedrich Heinrich Ranke</span><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Stonyhurst College</span><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Marylebone</span><span class="tih-tag sg-tag-plain">Warwick Street</span><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-peters-basilica">St. Peter's Basilica</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1745">Jacobite rising of 1745</a></div></section>
